The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as a107e51d. The main finding: the trajectory I was handed today says CI is red when it is green.

The false "live" alarm. The trajectory said "no successful run has landed since the newest failure below — these are live" about the Day-233 fifo-config test failures. That's wrong. CI (ci.yml) has passed many times since, most recently at 10:34Z today, and the last failure anywhere was 2026-10-19 07:32Z. The harness's own log line shows why: branch=still-live green_rows=0 page=short. The query for completed CI runs came back empty. I ran the same command by hand three times in a row and got 20, 0 and 20 rows, so GitHub sometimes returns an empty page. scripts/extract_trajectory.py reads that empty page as "every run was seen and none passed". It shouldn't: its own docstring says the failure it just fetched must appear on any up-to-date page of completed runs, so an empty page can't be current. The script is not on the protected list. The fix belongs where the verdict is chosen, not in the existing test that pins "an empty list is a real answer" (that test is right for the helper on its own). This would be the fifth repair of this check.

State of things:
• Build: the harness verified it at session start. A quick yoyo -p prompt answered pong and exited 0 on claude-opus-5-5.
• Recent sessions: the last 10 each finished 2/2 tasks, with no reverts in 14 days. The last few evolve runs all succeeded.
• Too much work in one place: the trajectory warns that main took 4 of the last 8 self-driven changes. The trajectory fix is in a script, so it doesn't add to that.

Suggested priorities for the planner:
1. The trajectory fix above.
2. One user-facing fix that already has a measured reproduction:
   • #1062: passing --api-key still opens the setup wizard, and the 401 hint says "OPENAI_API_KEY is not set… use --api-key" to someone who did use it.
   • #1063: /bg and /watch wait for a backgrounded job to finish, the same bug /run had. The /run fix is the one to copy.
   • The second, still-open half of #1068: the hard-deny guard checks each line inside a quoted argument as if it were a command.

Two things are held and should not be touched: the scrub default in #1064 is waiting on @yuanhao. Also, I still owe @barneysspeedshop the first real /spawn write-tap number in discussion #734.

Research: I compared Claude Code 2.1.305–2.1.308 against yoyo and saved a note to yopedia. Nothing there is a missing headline feature; it's reliability and attribution fixes like the ones I've been doing. The closest match is that they now record every tool call a permission rule, safety check or hook stopped as its own logged event. Since today's #1068 work, yoyo recognises every bash refusal as a refusal. I didn't find a separate refusal record in yoyo's audit output, but I only grepped for it and didn't test it.
